{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqgtvw168ex","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"headless-drains shipped to main; daemon restart required to go live","summary":"The headless-drains feature is merged to main (main HEAD 8e9024a; 5 files, +1604/-31: lib/headless-drain.js runner+governor+3 drain consumers, lib/claude-cli.js shared resolver, daemon.js unref'd setInterval trigger, scripts/onboard-learn.js refactor, test/headless-drain.test.js 40 tests). All three standing drains (learner, judge, label) now run as daemon-spawned headless processes under one opt-in governor. ORCH_HEADLESS_DRAINS=1 is set durably in BOTH .mcp.json env (mcp-graph.js self-boot path) and .claude/settings.json env (SessionStart start-daemon.js hook path). NOT YET LIVE: the currently-running daemon still has the OLD code (no drain trigger) and the flag is read at boot, so activation requires a daemon RESTART (kill the process listening on :8787, then let it reboot with the new code + flag). The restart could not be performed from the agent session — the shell could not spawn for process control (EPERM on powershell.exe, even with sandbox disabled). Per system convention a daemon restart is a deliberate manual step anyway. To activate: kill :8787 and relaunch node daemon.js (or kill it and restart the Claude session so start-daemon.js reboots it). First headless drain tick fires within ~5 min of the restart; watch the dashboard / new judge-journal shadow rows as evidence.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-16T16:00:06.378Z","vec":[-0.07317918539047241,0.009446848183870316,-0.051946867257356644,0.024871893227100372,0.04051065817475319,-0.035269029438495636,-0.03874053806066513,0.05103997886180878,0.007078080903738737,0.07963347434997559,0.0110354945063591,0.05258721485733986,-0.02376490831375122,0.007086374796926975,-0.034402601420879364,0.010268757119774818,0.01894397661089897,-0.03778625652194023,-0.012863344512879848,0.014877247624099255,0.042681820690631866,-0.054797302931547165,0.030124